    <section class="section" id="backend">
      <div class="container backend-layout">
        <div class="stack">
          <article class="card">
            <span class="badge">Authentication</span>
            <h2 style="margin-top:1rem">Supabase backend structure</h2>
            <p style="margin-top:1rem">Supabase’s JavaScript reference shows that authentication is managed from the `supabase.auth` namespace after you initialize the client with your project URL and publishable key, so I added a real integration block for sign-up, sign-in, and sign-out wiring [web:32][web:33][web:45].</p>
            <div class="api-grid" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
              <div class="status">Backend provider: Supabase</div>
              <div class="status">Auth flow: Email/password</div>
              <div class="status">Session mode: In-browser client session</div>
              <div class="status">Next step: Add your project keys</div>
            </div>
            <div class="code-block" style="margin-top:1rem">import { createClient } from 'https://esm.sh/@supabase/supabase-js@2'
const supabase = createClient(SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY)

await supabase.auth.signUp({ email, password })
await supabase.auth.signInWithPassword({ email, password })
await supabase.auth.signOut()</div>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="badge">Payment gateway</span>
            <h3 style="margin-top:1rem">Razorpay integration structure</h3>
            <p>Razorpay’s standard web checkout guide says you should create an account, generate test API keys, build the integration, test it, and then complete the go-live checklist, so the right production path is to create orders on your backend and launch checkout from the frontend [web:40][web:43].</p>
            <div class="code-block" style="margin-top:1rem">POST /api/create-order
  → server creates Razorpay order
  → frontend opens Razorpay Checkout with order_id
  → server verifies payment signature before activation</div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <article class="card">
          <span class="badge">Live setup panel</span>
          <h2 style="margin-top:1rem">Connect your backend</h2>
          <form id="backendForm" class="stack" style="margin-top:1rem">
            <div class="field"><label for="supabaseUrl">Supabase URL</label><input id="supabaseUrl" placeholder="https://your-project.supabase.co"></div>
